# App conventions (living list)

Append new bullets here when a pattern must be reused across the project. Do not re-implement these helpers inline.

## Path slugs (`src/lib/paths.ts`)

API or CMS slugs may contain `&`, `?`, `#`, or spaces. Those characters **break** the URL if interpolated raw (`/topics/agriculture-&-food` is parsed as path + query).

- **Build hrefs** with path helpers that call `encodePathSlug` (e.g. `paths.article(slug)`, `paths.category(slug)`). Do not concatenate slugs into path strings yourself.
- **Read route params** (and any slug from the URL) with **`decodePathSlug`**. Never `decodeURIComponent` ad hoc; never compare the raw param to a stored slug without decoding.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const href = `/articles/${item.slug}`;
items.find((f) => f.slug === params.slug);

// ✅ GOOD
import { decodePathSlug, paths } from "@/lib/paths";
const href = paths.article(item.slug);
const slug = decodePathSlug(params.slug);
```

Prefer a shared resolver (e.g. `findBySlug`) that already uses `decodePathSlug` when matching list data to a route param.
